    <Byline publishedDate="2026-07-04" updatedDate="2026-07-04" />

    <div class="bg-secondary/40 border-l-4 border-primary rounded-r-lg px-5 py-4 mb-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground mb-1">Direct Answer</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Tall users need monitor arms with a maximum height extension of 20"–28" above the desk surface, depending on height and desk height. Most consumer arms max out at 15"–20" — insufficient above 6'2" in most setups. The calculation: seated eye level minus desk height gives the required top-of-monitor position above the desk. Verify this against the arm's published maximum height before purchasing.</p>
    </div>

